sumer needs membership changes reflected; source currently shows no recovering-state check in stepNode and no shared snapshotLock. This is more concrete than exploring ungrounded combinations of old read confirmations across membership changes.',disposition='needs_specific_evidence',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\nlookup={x['id']:x for x in m['behaviors']+m['facts']};q['source_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(s for i in q['behavior_ids']+q['fact_ids']+list(q['supporting_behavior_ids']) for s in lookup[i]['source_ids']))\njson.dump(m,open('map_recovery.json','w'),indent=2)\ns=dict(action='continue',map_path='map_recovery.json',map_changes=changes,question=q,sources=news,rationale='Reselect the concrete snapshot-publication authority premise after the read correlation finding is confirmed. Save the answered read relationship and the ordinary-batch protection at this related map handoff; do not claim a snapshot defect yet.',feedback=dict(ref_ids=['c611aead474d4b8fa96906fb00bd1771','808ff406433543c6b00ac285959caed1','B-read-confirm','B-apply','B-recovery','B-authority','src-visible-applied','src-rsm-batch-order','src-rsm-recover-entry'],answered='Controller assessment confirms the scoped read-prefix identity violation after correspondence review. Ordinary applied-index publication was then traced: setApplied only advances internal index/term; setLastApplied publishes the visible index after handleEntry returns, so ApplyConfigChange precedes visibility. Snapshot recovery differs: apply writes lastApplied before Recover calls RestoreRemotes; the latter competes for raftMu with the initialized node step worker. This leaves a distinct sourced authority-transition question, without assuming that the available locks fail in a legal history.',remaining=['Construct a legal initialized snapshot recovery overlap and inspect whether an election uses old membership.','Pending read-support eligibility across membership changes remains a separate unresolved surface; fixed-membership observers cannot generate nonzero read-confirmation replies because those heartbeats target only voting members.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Retain the confirmed result without rerunning it; source ordering supplies a new discriminator and explains the ordinary-batch alternative.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-06_19-33-36-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
